# ISO 14064-1 Compliance Implementation Plan

# Goal Description
Implement the missing ISO 14064-1 features identified in the compliance audit: **Uncertainty Assessment**, **Verification Workflow**, and **Biogenic CO2 Separation**. This will elevate the tool from EPA-compliant to enterprise-ready.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Migration**: This change will alter the `emissions` and `custom_factors` tables. Existing records will default to: `uncertainty=0`, `status='verified'`, `co2_biogenic=0`.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend ([server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/server.js))
#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/server.js)
*   **Database Schema**:
    *   Add `uncertainty` (REAL) and `status` (TEXT) and `co2_biogenic` (REAL) to `emissions` table.
    *   Add `uncertainty` (REAL) to `custom_factors` table.
*   **API Endpoints**:
    *   Update `POST /api/emissions` to accept `uncertainty`, `status`, and `biogenic_co2` fields.
    *   Update `POST /api/factors` to accept `uncertainty`.
    *   Update `POST /api/emissions/:id/status` (New Endpoint) for the verification workflow (approve/reject).

### Frontend (User Interface)
#### [MODIFY] [public/js/emissions-calc.js] (Assuming file exists based on audit) OR [public/index.html]
*   **Emissions Form**:
    *   Add input field for **Uncertainty (±%)**.
    *   Add toggle or auto-calc for **Biogenic CO2**.
    *   Add "Submit for Approval" vs "Save Draft" buttons.
*   **Dashboard/Table**:
    *   Display "Draft" vs "Verified" badges on records.
    *   Show Uncertainty ± values in the table.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
*   **Database Check**: Verify new columns exist in [users_v2.db](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/users_v2.db) (or user specific db) after server restart.
*   **API Test**: Send a POST request with the new fields and verify they are stored and returned.

### Manual Verification
1.  Create a new emission record with 5% uncertainty and "Draft" status.
2.  Verify it appears in the dashboard with a "Draft" badge.
3.  "Approve" the record and verify status changes to "Verified".
